:level-1
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 1"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Primary Education Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Primary Education Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Basic knowledge in literacy, numeracy, and communication.
- Awareness of civic, moral, and cultural values.

Skills:
- Basic cognitive, communication, practical, and problem-solving skills.
- Apply basic and creative reasoning.
- Reflective and critical thinking.
- Show competency to use basic mathematical and ICT tools.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Structured learning environments but gradually develop the ability to think critically, ability to work collaboratively, and take age-appropriate independence and decision-making within guided settings.
- Applies an elementary understanding of appropriate values, attitudes and ethics.

Duration:
- 6 years.
"""@en ;
.

:level-2
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 2"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Secondary Education Ordinary Level Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Secondary Education Ordinary Level Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Holistic comprehension and application of factual and operational knowledge.

Skills:
- Intermediate communication, cognitive, and practical skills to apply knowledge in solving non-complex problems within structured and familiar contexts.
- Use a few simple/basic applications, which are adequate to perform given task(s) under guidance.
- Critical thinking, creativity, and adaptability while fostering technical competencies, problem-solving skills.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Gradual independence, transitioning from structured supervision to increasing responsibility in varied practical settings for individual and group tasks.
- Informed decision-making.
- Applies basic understanding of the values, attitudes and ethics in carrying out basic tasks.

Duration:
- 4 years.
"""@en ;
.

:level-3
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 3"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Level 3 Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Level 3 Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Factual, technical, operational, and theoretical knowledge within a specific area of work and learning.

Skills:
- Interpret, apply and communicate solutions to familiar and predictable problems.
- Communicate within a limited range of contexts requiring simple and direct exchange of information on familiar and routine matters.
- Use a limited range of basic applications and digital tools which are adequate to perform a given set of task(s) under supervision that enables access, and to process simple data.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Functions independently in predictable contexts under routine supervision and guidance, with initiative for self-responsibility and some responsibility for group outcomes.
- Applies simple understanding of the values, attitudes and ethics in a subject field or discipline to carry out selected tasks.

Duration:
- 1 year (1200 Notional Hours, 120 Credits) or through RPL.
"""@en ;
.

:level-4
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 4"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Secondary Education Advanced Level Certificate"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Level 4 Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification types: Secondary Education Advanced Level Certificate; Level 4 Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Factual, operational, technical and theoretical knowledge.
- Theory and practical applications, critical thinking and analytical reasoning.

Skills:
- Use of well-developed technical skills to make informed judgments, and apply solutions and problem-solving analytical abilities in both familiar and unfamiliar situations.
- Communicate effectively and clearly orally or in writing, ideas, information, problems and solutions, individually or as a team to peers, experts and non-experts.
- Use basic digital technology applications to support study/work to seek and process data related to a subject of study/work.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Varied (predictable and unpredictable) contexts with adaptability, independent and collaborative decision making and initiative for self-direction under general guidance, accountability and taking full responsibility for self, some planning and responsibility for group outcomes and initiative for responsibility for others.
- Applies a general understanding of the values, attitudes and ethics required in a subject field or discipline and displays these to others.

Duration:
- Secondary Education Advanced Level Certificate: 2 years (2400 Notional Hours, 240 Credits).
- Level 4 Certificate: 2 years (2400 Notional Hours, 240 Credits) or through RPL.
"""@en ;
.

:level-5
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 5"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Level 5 Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Level 5 Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Substantial depth in technical or theoretical knowledge with the ability to integrate facts, operational insights, and theoretical frameworks to address complex, unfamiliar problems.
- Some level of specialisation in areas of expertise.

Skills:
- Well-developed technical and analytical skills to synthesise information, construct well-reasoned arguments, and apply a range of solutions to complex issues.
- Communicate clearly, both orally and in writing, ideas, information, problems and solutions, to others including peers, experts and non-experts.
- Use a range of digital applications to support study/work as well as to seek and process data related to work or study.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Unpredictable contexts with full autonomy and full responsibility for self and group outcomes, and some responsibility for others.
- Shows a broad understanding of the values, attitudes and ethics associated with the occupation and/or study and displays these to others.

Duration:
- 2½ years (3000 Notional Hours, 300 Credits) or through RPL.
"""@en ;
.

:level-6
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 6"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Diploma"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Diploma.

Knowledge:
- Advanced technical or theoretical knowledge in specialised areas of work or study, able to adapt and formulate solutions for complex or abstract problems using up-to-date principles and theories.

Skills:
- Advanced, specialised skills to collate, analyse, synthesise, and communicate information clearly.
- Communicate and interact effectively and cogently in a comprehensive and well-structured manner to convey information, ideas, problems and solutions for social, academic and professional purposes to a range of audiences.
- Use a range of information, media and technology applications to support study and/or work.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Highly variable contexts with well-developed autonomy in managing self and others to meet objectives.
- Responsibility for processes and resources, including ensuring that complex solutions are implemented effectively.
- Demonstrates significant understanding of the values, attitudes and ethics associated with the occupation and/or study and introduces these to others.

Duration:
- 2 years (2400 Notional Hours, 240 Credits) - 3 years (3600 Notional Hours, 360 Credits) or through RPL.
"""@en ;
.

:level-7
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 7"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Bachelor's Degree"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Bachelor's Degree.

Knowledge:
- Advanced analytical and/or specialised knowledge of a discipline, contributing new insights and frameworks.

Skills:
- Able to devise tailored solutions for unfamiliar issues, demonstrating proficiency in specialised fields.
- Highly specialised and advanced skills to generate new insights, formulate innovative solutions, and contribute to theoretical and practical advancements in the discipline.
- Convey ideas both in written or oral forms using appropriate and different forms of presentation, confidently, accurately and coherently in appropriate context in a well-structured manner to a diversity of audiences.
- Use a broad range of information, media and technology applications to support study and/or work.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Complex, variable contexts with significant autonomy and responsibility for outcomes.
- Manages teams, resources, and processes to ensure successful implementation.
- Applies advanced knowledge of the associated values, attitudes and ethics and encourages the use of these in others.

Duration:
- 3 years (3600 Notional Hours, 360 Credits) - 6 years (7200 Notional Hours, 720 Credits).
"""@en ;
.

:level-8
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 8"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Bachelor Honours Degree"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Postgraduate Diploma"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Postgraduate Certificate"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification types: Bachelor Honours Degree; Postgraduate Diploma; Postgraduate Certificate.

Knowledge:
- Highly advanced and complex body of knowledge, including cutting-edge theories, principles, and methodologies.

Skills:
- Able to engage in advanced problem-solving within the field.
- Highly advanced skills to critically analyse and synthesise information, demonstrating the ability to innovate and lead in theoretical and practical advancements.
- Proficiency in developing and testing new solutions through research.
- Communicate clearly the knowledge, skills, ideas, critique and conclusion/rationale using appropriate methods to peers, experts, and non-experts.
- Competently use a wide range of suitable digital technologies and appropriate software to enhance study, research and/or work/practice.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- High levels of autonomy and responsibility, ensuring that outcomes are achieved in specialised and complex contexts.
- Advanced leadership in managing resources, processes, and teams, fostering innovation.

Duration:
- Bachelor Honours Degree: 1 year (1200 Notional Hours, 120 Credits).
- Postgraduate Diploma: 1 year (1200 Notional Hours, 120 Credits).
- Postgraduate Certificate: Min. 6 months (min. 600 Notional Hours, min. 60 Credits).
"""@en ;
.

:level-9
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 9"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Master's Degree"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Master's Degree.

Knowledge:
- Mastery of a complex body of knowledge at the forefront of research and innovation, contributing to new theories, models, and frameworks.
- Ability to integrate cross-disciplinary perspectives to address emergent issues.

Skills:
- Skills mastery required to demonstrate originality and new insights in research and/or innovation and formulate and test theories to show mastery of highly complex, abstract problems.
- Communicate clearly the knowledge, skills, ideas, critique and conclusion/rationale using appropriate methods to peers, experts, and non-experts.
- Competently use a wide range of suitable digital technologies and appropriate software to enhance study, research and/or work/practice.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Expertise in managing and leading in highly specialised contexts.
- Holds full responsibility for resources, teams, and outcomes, influencing and guiding stakeholders to advance the field.

Duration:
- 1 year (1200 Notional Hours, 120 Credits) - 4 years (4800 Notional Hours, 480 Credits).
"""@en ;
.

:level-10
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme   acqf-qcp-model:zm-nqf-levels ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Level 10"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Doctorate Degree"@en ;
    skos:definition """
Qualification type: Doctorate Degree.

Knowledge:
- Original knowledge that reshapes or significantly extends the forefront of a discipline, contributing to its evolution.
- Capable of bridging multiple disciplines to address emergent challenges.

Skills:
- Supremacy at innovation, creating new theoretical frameworks, testing hypotheses, and addressing emerging problems.
- Communicate effectively research findings to peers, scholarly communities and society at large in the relevant field of expertise.
- Use/select/improve existing or develop new appropriate tools/methodologies to support and enhance research activities.
- Able to lead multidisciplinary teams and guide the creation of new knowledge.
- Capable of leading transformative changes across disciplines.

Autonomy and responsibility:
- Highest level of autonomy and leadership in emergent and dynamic contexts, with full responsibility for strategic direction, managing resources, processes, and outcomes.
- Provides visionary leadership and shapes future directions in the discipline.

Duration:
- Min. 3 years (min. 3600 Notional Hours, min. 360 Credits).
"""@en ;
.
